{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/551311-kindred-influence-ghouls-and-blood-puppets-and-the-masquerade","id":551311,"title":"Kindred Influence, Ghouls and Blood Puppets and the Masquerade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-12T06:34:22-07:00","id":551311,"title":"Kindred Influence, Ghouls and Blood Puppets and the Masquerade","content":"Hi there. <br /> <br /> Since - The Requiem came out - I\u00b4m thinking a lot about the distinction between Ghouls and just &quot;plain&quot; blood-addicted mortals. <br /> Especially in contrast to kindred influence in the world of mortals and keeping the Masquerade intact. <br /> <br /> My conclusion was that making ghouls is something vampires rarely do or just in special circumstances.<br /> <br /> Regarding Influence - it\u00b4s better to have unknowing or maybe just a simple bloodpuppet. Because the vinculum and thus the obedience is that what a vampire wants. She does not really want an undying agent of hers in a visible position. <br /> <br /> Ghouling the chief of police or similiar persons of high influence is quite risk to the masquerade. The chief of police is really hooked on that he meets regular and he can\u00b4t deny when she wants him to cover up a strange homicide. <br /> <br /> But why have ghouls(?): <br /> * You need powerful agents for your masquerade or for daylight activity. Be it the classic ghouls bounce with vigor or the high society socialite with supernatural charme. <br /> *companionship - they can be a link to your mortal past - but always stay with you.<br /> * guilt - you almost killed someone - and the only solution was to make them a ghoul. <br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on this?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:32:06-07:00","id":551411,"title":"","content":"It depends on the vampire in question. Some vampires might see no reason to make the distinction between those they ghoul, and those they submit to the vinculum. Some may have large stables of ghouls. Some might never want to have a ghoul, but are free with the blood addiction / bonds. <br /> <br /> What you came up with is good for the justification of one vampire. Maybe a group, or popular theme in vampire circles. I don't think that any kind of philosophy regarding the ghouls can be made so generic, though. Vampires are still individuals, who will approach the issue in different ways. <br /> <br /> Hells. There may be Lancea et Sanctum vampires who ghoul sinners as part of their &quot;divine predation&quot; and keep a large number of them - the ghouls comprise the entire Herd. In Circle, well, circles, ghouls can become members of an acolyte's coven - there's no reason they can't be taught enough Cruac to assist in the group rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:13:37-07:00","id":551654,"title":"","content":"Yes you made some good points. And it\u00b4s interesting how your examples are more directly adding to a vampire or a covenant, but my point was that. mortal pawns in visible positions are not really helping much if they are ghouls in the long run before they tend to risk the masquerade by not aging. <br /> <br /> Of course you could put a ghouls several years into withdrawal to keep him aging but it\u00b4s another risk as mistreatment might shatter the vinculum and also a ghouls in withdrawal unpredictable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:33:58-07:00","id":551882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/551311-kindred-influence-ghouls-and-blood-puppets-and-the-masquerade?p=551654#post551654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes you made some good points. And it\u00b4s interesting how your examples are more directly adding to a vampire or a covenant, but my point was that. mortal pawns in visible positions are not really helping much if they are ghouls in the long run before they tend to risk the masquerade by not aging.</div> </div> </div> </div> I find the assumption that vampires care about mortal pawns in visible positions to be shaky in the first place. While there are a notable number who do care, especially in the Invictus and Movement, there are quite a number who don't. There are plenty of options where mortal pawns have nothing to do with visible positions at all. <br /> <br /> There's also the issue that many vampires don't aim specifically for direct controlling of the people in power, but for those who influence the people in power (ie - you ghoul the secretary, who is there to whisper in the ear, but never stands in the light, and stays there while everyone else comes and goes, and no one questions how long she's been there).<br /> <br /> I brought up the Lance and Circle bit for showing that there are other uses for a ghoul than as mortal pawn. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course you could put a ghouls several years into withdrawal to keep him aging but it\u00b4s another risk as mistreatment might shatter the vinculum and also a ghouls in withdrawal unpredictable. </div> </div> </div> That defeats the purpose of a ghouling, doesn't it? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}